---
/** A rubber-stamp tag, the notebook's bounded all-caps exception (BRAND.md, DESIGN.md "Notebook
 * ink system"): a framed mono 600 label at 13 px or more, at most two words and 12 characters,
 * tilted a few degrees. The text arrives through the slot and must come from i18n (it is already
 * capitalized there, nothing here transforms the case). The stamp is decorative reinforcement of a
 * label that exists elsewhere, so it is `aria-hidden`; place it with a class from the parent
 * (`absolute` over a corner, for instance), since the component owns the look and not the position.
 *
 * `tone` picks the ink: `pink` (default) or `primary`. Both are semantic tokens. The entrance
 * "lands" once (300 ms, transform only, never opacity, no layout shift) and is off under
 * `prefers-reduced-motion`. The look lives in `stamp.css`, not in a scoped `<style>`: a component
 * reached through a feature barrel (as the decision record is) would ship its scoped CSS to every
 * page that imports the barrel. A page that renders a stamp inlines `stamp.css?inline` in its head
 * (NotePage does), so only that page pays for it. */
type Props = { tone?: 'pink' | 'primary'; class?: string };

const { tone = 'pink', class: className } = Astro.props;
---

<span data-stamp class:list={['stamp', `stamp-${tone}`, className]} aria-hidden="true"><slot /></span>
